{
  "_comment": [
    "The availability plan, authoring plan Step 2: where every evolution line on the",
    "species pick-list is meant to be caught, decided on paper before any slot is",
    "written. Keyed by area so Step 3 can read a table's intended cast straight off",
    "it; docs/oxide/encounters/availability.md is the per-line view, generated from",
    "this file by `cli availability --write` and never edited by hand.",
    "",
    "Each area lists lines by their first stage's constant. `home` is where the line",
    "is guaranteed (its first stage at 10% or more of the merged share, authoring",
    "plan decision 3); `cameo` is any other appearance, at any share and any stage,",
    "which is where R13's variety and the dupe-out structure come from. A line has",
    "one home. Lines with a gift, trade, static battle, starter or fossil script",
    "need no home and are listed only as cameos. `water` names the surf or rod",
    "tables that are a water line's home, since the design scoped land first and",
    "those tables get a no-leak pass in Step 5.",
    "",
    "The corridor (every area up to and including `corridor_end`) carries only",
    "starter-adjacent lines and lines with a scripted source, and every",
    "starter-adjacent line's home is in the corridor. `cli availability` checks",
    "both, and that each early-band table has three to five lines planned.",
    "",
    "Multi-room areas (Old Chateau, Lost Tower, Solaceon Ruins, Great Marsh, Iron",
    "Island, Mt Coronet, Turnback Cave and its twenty-five post-game rooms) share a",
    "cast and vary it room by room; the home is on the room named. Hand-edited on",
    "purpose: this is the design, and it is Ian's to change."
  ],
